    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f0e024c8_b16359bd",
        "filename": "cmd/multiproduct_kati/main.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074628
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-20T01:22:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s just \"--dist\", not --dist\u003dtrue. That matches the \u0027dist\u0027 argument normally passed to the build, and how the dist dir actually gets selected (notice that this is using the normal build config struct to get the dist dir).\n\nThere\u0027s also a loose convention about what the dist dir contains -- artifacts are at the top, and there\u0027s a logs subdirectory that has a few files that the buildbot will write to. So soong_ui sticks logs about how it executed the build into that directory (including the trace), but everything else goes into the top level.\n\nWe really never expect users to use dist, unless they\u0027re attempting to imitate the build server. So the default without any arguments produces sane user defaults -- all the output goes into a timestamp-based folder under your current output directory.\n\nThe only reason I could see a user wanting to move the logs elsewhere is so that they can preserve the logs but remove the large ninja files. But I think that\u0027s better handled by having an option similar to keep that keeps successful logs but delete the rest of the intermediates once they\u0027re done. Then everything for one build is still in one spot without any paths to manage.",
      "parentUuid": "70595a0c_1663466a",
      "revId": "5a76aa22aabbc4ca8cecbb6ee51a122ea9528ad0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fceb32eb_f4972ed8",
        "filename": "cmd/multiproduct_kati/main.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137668
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-22T18:26:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh ok. Yeah I\u0027m less interested in exactly making the log directory configurable and more interested in deduplicating the logic about where it goes (and more generally what \u0027dist\u0027 means).\n\nAre there any builds where both OutDir and DistDir are expected to be used? It seems to me that it if making the \u0027logs\u0027 subdirectory is standard for a \u0027dist\u0027 build, then we\u0027d instead want a method on Config called perhaps \u0027turnYourselfIntoADistBuild\u0027 (probably abbreviated something like \u0027BeDist\u0027 or just \u0027Dist\u0027 (I wanted \u0027MakeDist\u0027 but \u0027make\u0027 seems like a confusing term here)) that both deduplicates these little pieces of configuration and also conveniently enumerates the full meaning of \u0027dist\u0027. Then I imagine we could call \u0027LogDir\u0027 if we do something like:\n\nfunc (c *config) BeDist() {\n  c.smartTerminal \u003d false\n  c.logSubdir \u003d \u0027logs\u0027\n  // are there more flags to activate by \"dist\" than this?\n}\n\nfunc (c *config) BeDistAt(dir string) {\n  c.beDist()\n  c.outDir \u003d dir\n}\n\nfunc (c *config) LogDir() (dir string) {\n  return path.join(c.OutDir(), c.logSubdir)\n}",
      "parentUuid": "f0e024c8_b16359bd",
      "revId": "5a76aa22aabbc4ca8cecbb6ee51a122ea9528ad0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "716be828_d8ad08c2",
        "filename": "cmd/multiproduct_kati/main.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074628
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-22T19:56:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "DistDir is separate from OutDir, and dist doesn\u0027t imply smartTerminal or not. The only \"standard\" thing it modifies is the directory for the main log and trace, but since there\u0027s only two implementations of that so far, it doesn\u0027t seem like a high priority to refactor that (and not simple either, we don\u0027t currently have the Config or Context change any settings for the logger or tracer -- they don\u0027t even have an interface that contains the necessary functions)\n\nThe implementations already need to know about dist vs not -- on the normal build, it\u0027s another build target that copies outputs from the output directory to the dist directory. For this implementation, we share the common move of the core log file, but all the other configs that we generate do something custom (different subdirectories under dist, without the standard logs directory).",
      "parentUuid": "fceb32eb_f4972ed8",
      "revId": "5a76aa22aabbc4ca8cecbb6ee51a122ea9528ad0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "96895428_bf73ae5f",
        "filename": "cmd/multiproduct_kati/main.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137668
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-22T21:45:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why would a caller want to have the log dir in another spot? Is it for a build server that wants to easily report back all the error logs by just using a single file glob to match all the log files? Is it that we want the logs to not be present in the final built artifact\u0027s root directory?\n\nFor the ability to rearrange the artifacts of the individual builds based on the \u0027dist\u0027 argument, can we simplify it by just always generating a structure that is suitable for what callers of \u0027dist\u0027 expect? Something like:\n\nlogs/sailfish/soong.log\nlogs/sailfish/build.trace\nlogs/bullhead/soong.log\nlogs/bullhead/build.trace\nsailfish/soong.log -\u003e ../../logs/sailfish/soong.log\nsailfish/build.trace -\u003e ../../logs/sailfish/build.trace\nsailfish/artifacts\nbullhead/logs/soong.log -\u003e ../../logs/bullhead/soong.log\nbullhead/logs/build.trace -\u003e ../../logs/bullhead/build.trace\nbullhead/artifacts\n\nThat also makes it easier to know in the future which files are candidates for remote caching: everything under */artifacts is intended to be unchanging between builds\n\nIf we do the above, then I imagine we\u0027d do similarly for the log dir on line 214.\n\n(If not, then I imagine we would deduplicate the getting of the path rather than the setting. It looks to me like we can just add a method in config.go on the configImpl type called getLogDir() that is called both on line 214 below and also on line 74 of soong_ui/main.go\n\nI\u0027m imagining the main advantage of this to be that it makes it easier to know what Dist() does (with the fact that it also deduplicates code being only a secondary advantage).)",
      "parentUuid": "716be828_d8ad08c2",
      "revId": "5a76aa22aabbc4ca8cecbb6ee51a122ea9528ad0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
